Is what I am doing bringing me closer to my current core goals?
I a while a go added a [[/now][/now]] section to the blog to help align all or most of what I did towards
my current major goals. But did that help? No. Why did it not.

I mean, it did. I thought more about the major goals than I usually do. So that's a plus.
But I had no actionable plan for what I was going to have to do daily to achieve those
goals. I therefore kept doing whatever it is I was doing. Productive work that did not
get me what I wanted long term but.. felt productive.

Also, I think I don't know what I want to become. I am not sure if my /now defined well enough if at all.
Do I want to become anything? Or to make
money? As in, am i really interested in becoming a Systems Engineer or in making enough
money to push me out of the rat race. Fastest most efficient way, top way. 

#+begin_quote
/If you have to choose, and this is an important decision to make:/
/Is it getting huge sums of money and checking out so as to do what you are *really* 
interested in or.. becoming "someone" in your slow growing profession that you are interested in./
#+end_quote

I was looking at Marc Lou's blog a few minutes ago. Indie dev is what I think he does.
I rememeber looking into the same after I just left school and making up my mind
to learn app development just for that. Where that goal fell I don't rememeber.

Problem? Consistency.

Reframing.

